rockchip: soc: declare CONFIG_CPU_RK3568 (vendor CPU selector)

The back-ported vendor video codec stack (MPP/RKV, patch 317) keeps the
vendor's per-SoC guards in mpp_rkvdec2.c.  The of_device_id table
(drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_rkvdec2.c:1325) contains:

    { .compatible = "rockchip,rkv-decoder-v2",     .data = &rkvdec_v2_data },
    #ifdef CONFIG_CPU_RK3568
    { .compatible = "rockchip,rkv-decoder-rk3568", .data = &rkvdec_rk3568_data },
    #endif

so the Panther X2's "rockchip,rkv-decoder-rk3568" node only reaches the
RK3566/8 data path when CONFIG_CPU_RK3568 is defined.

In the rockchip vendor kernel that symbol is declared in
drivers/soc/rockchip/Kconfig.cpu, which is sourced from
drivers/soc/rockchip/Kconfig and holds:

    menu "Rockchip CPU selection"
        depends on ARCH_ROCKCHIP
        ...
        config CPU_RK3568
            bool "RK3566/8"
        ...
    endmenu

and enabled from arch/arm64/configs/rockchip_defconfig.  This tree never
imported Kconfig.cpu, so CONFIG_CPU_RK3568 is undefined, the rk3568
of_match entry is compiled out, and rkvdec2 attaches the generic
"rockchip,rkv-decoder-v2" data (rkvdec_v2_data):

  * hack_setup is never set  -> rkvdec2_rk3568_alloc_task()/run() are not
    used, need_hack stays 0, dec->fix is never allocated,
  * the link register layout is the v2 one, which does not match the
    RK3566/8 hardware (LINK_EN never latches).

Result: no HEVC decode (diagnostics show fix 0x0 / link_en 0x0).

This patch declares the missing selector in drivers/soc/rockchip/Kconfig
with the vendor's semantics (plain bool, default n, enabled per target via
the kernel config), and target/linux/rockchip/armv8/config-5.4 turns it on.
No code changes: rkvdec_rk3568_data/rkvdec2_rk3568_{init,exit,alloc_task,
run} and rkvdec_rk3568_{hw,dev}_ops are already defined unconditionally, so
enabling the macro only re-enables the of_match entry.

--- a/drivers/soc/rockchip/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/soc/rockchip/Kconfig
@@ -5,6 +5,20 @@
 # Rockchip Soc drivers
 #
 
+#
+# Rockchip CPU selection
+#
+# Plain bool SoC selectors consumed by the vendor video codec (MPP/RKV)
+# driver to pick its per-SoC data path.  Mirrors the vendor develop-5.10/6.6
+# tree's drivers/soc/rockchip/Kconfig.cpu (menu "Rockchip CPU selection");
+# only the RK3566/RK3568 selector is needed here: mpp_rkvdec2.c gates the
+# "rockchip,rkv-decoder-rk3568" of_match entry on CONFIG_CPU_RK3568, whose
+# absence made rkvdec2 fall back to the generic v2 data path (hack_setup=0,
+# no dec->fix, wrong link layout).
+#
+config CPU_RK3568
+	bool "RK3566/8"
+
 config ROCKCHIP_GRF
 	bool "Rockchip General Register Files support" if COMPILE_TEST
 	default y if ARCH_ROCKCHIP
